diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Campus DNS service (BIND/named) on srv1 (10.5.0.4). Laptop1 is receiving DNS settings that point to this server.

Mechanism: Laptop1 has working L2/L3 to the WiFi gateway and beyond (eth0 10.6.0.100/24, default via 10.6.0.1; ping to 10.6.0.1 OK; ping to 10.5.0.4 OK). However, name resolution fails: resolv.conf on Laptop1 contains “nameserver 10.5.0.4” and getent hosts example.com returns no result; curl to example.com returns HTTP code 000 (DNS failure). The DNS daemon on srv1 is listening on 10.5.0.4:53 (named), but is configured as non-recursive/authoritative-only. Its /etc/bind/named.conf.options explicitly sets “recursion no;” and only serves a local zone (“jeremysitlab.com”). Thus any external 
